<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aargau</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Canton of Aargau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aargau is a region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aare">Aare</a>, Reuss and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limmat">Limmat</a>, today a canton with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aarau">Aarau</a>. It was the cradle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg dynasty</a>, whose ancestral castle stands near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brugg">Brugg</a>, until the Swiss Confederates, led by Bern, conquered it in 1415. Ruled for centuries as subject land of Bern and of the Confederates in common, it became a full canton under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-mediation">Act of Mediation</a> in 1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aargau.jpg" alt="Aargau" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AxG · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aargau.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
